The '''1996 FA Charity Shield''' (also known as the '''[[Littlewoods]] FA Charity Shield''' for sponsorship reasons) was the 74th [[FA Community Shield|FA Charity Shield]], an annual [[association football|football]] match played between the winners of the previous season's [[Premier League]] and [[FA Cup]] competitions. The match was played on 11 August 1996 at [[Wembley Stadium (1923)|Wembley Stadium]]<ref>{{cite news |title=Details - 1996/97 Charity Shield |url=https://www.footballsite.co.uk/Statistics/CommunityShield/1996-97CharityShield.htm |publisher=www.footballsite.co.uk}}</ref> and contested by [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]], who had won [[Double (association football)|the Double]] of [[1995–96 FA Premier League|Premier League]] and [[1995–96 FA Cup|FA Cup]] in 1995–96, and [[Newcastle United F.C.|Newcastle United]], who had finished as runners-up in the Premier League. Manchester United won the match 4–0 with goals from [[Eric Cantona]], [[Nicky Butt]], [[David Beckham]] and [[Roy Keane]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Best Community Shield matches |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/blog/name/93/post/1979238/headline |work=[[ESPN]] |date=9 August 2014 |language=en}}</ref>

The game saw new signings Jordi Cruyff and Karel Poborský make their debuts for Manchester United, though neither of these players had particularly successful careers at [[Old Trafford]] and both had left the club within four years. The day before the game had seen the surprise sale of one of Manchester United's longest serving players – [[Lee Sharpe]].

The game saw Newcastle United give a debut to £15 million world record signing [[Alan Shearer]], who would remain at the club until his retirement as a player 10 years later and break the club's goalscoring record in the process, though he would never win a [[major trophy]] with them.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Sunderland |first1=Tom |title=Community Shield: Revisiting the Last 25 Matches |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/2148884-community-shield-revisiting-the-last-25-matches |work=Bleacher Report |language=en}}</ref>

